    "skills": [
      {
        "id": "root-cause",
        "stages": [
          "investigate"
        ],
        "text": "# root-cause\n\nTrace a failing example from the written contract to the current implementation. Explain the mechanism of the defect before proposing a repair. Consider whether several symptoms share one cause.\n",
        "sha256": "d7e39a3d95ef179714494c10c5c6d83860d5a9795ec4b4aad06051c943ebe565"
      },
      {
        "id": "minimal-fix",
        "stages": [
          "implement"
        ],
        "text": "# minimal-fix\n\nPreserve public names and signatures. Prefer a small, direct repair and avoid unrelated abstractions or new dependencies. Check that the small repair still satisfies the complete written contract.\n",
        "sha256": "4ab3951990949b940f5e90ba3d9f96f6f76778d781ce66f4877948c27d2b7dc2"
      },
      {
        "id": "edge-cases",
        "stages": [
          "verify"
        ],
        "text": "# edge-cases\n\nReview empty inputs, single elements, repeated values, boundary values, and invalid inputs described by the contract. Try a counterexample to the proposed algorithm, rather than relying only on a happy-path example.\n",
        "sha256": "43664d90652f9b08f3ec7bce22df12b8da711c5d8b94f5415aefdb950931be88"
      },
      {
        "id": "input-validation",
        "stages": [
          "investigate",
          "implement"
        ],
        "text": "# input-validation\n\nSeparate input validation from the main transformation. Validate the entire input when the contract requires invalid inputs to raise, even if an early lookup or a shortcut could otherwise return a result.\n",
        "sha256": "6923963fae4c90e128e5d453b32170fca331695672421f2818877415b7b327d3"
      },
      {
        "id": "compatibility",
        "stages": [
          "investigate",
          "verify"
        ],
        "text": "# compatibility\n\nTreat the public interface and documented exception types as compatibility requirements. Avoid mutating caller-owned inputs unless requested. Preserve behavior that the task does not ask to change.\n",
        "sha256": "58735c6e0466aea6510bd07310b6469a5dce0e64ee944b7c70a745ca32423ef7"
      },
      {
        "id": "python-idioms",
        "stages": [
          "implement"
        ],
        "text": "# python-idioms\n\nConsider standard-library and built-in tools before writing a broad custom framework. Sorting, sets, comprehensions, heapq, and regular expressions can simplify repairs. Check ordering, equality, escaping, and duplicate semantics before choosing an idiom.\n",
        "sha256": "6b61cebde3032224359a77c66128a96c0f61f0c58e3e15b7cd7cb1ed6e74594b"
      }
    ],
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "clamp",
        "split": "discovery",
        "instruction": "Fix `clamp(value, lower, upper)` for numeric inputs.\n\n- Return the value if it is inside the inclusive interval [lower, upper].\n- Return lower if the value is below the interval, or upper if above it.\n- If lower is greater than upper, raise ValueError rather than silently swapping them.\n- Preserve the function name and signature. Use the Python standard library only.\n",
        "starter": "def clamp(value, lower, upper):\n    return min(lower, max(value, upper))\n",
        "grader_sha256": "82d148112437b249025e43475b6234e42ea942c9779fb09c9b5e7fe368d68c98",
        "sha256": "f6e03e43b8a78cf24bd397a4f017df5bbeed1013ca453dc0c0a387c3c54edbac"
      },
      {
        "id": "merge-intervals",
        "split": "discovery",
        "instruction": "Repair merge_intervals(intervals). Each interval is a two-number list [start, end].\nReturn a new list sorted by start with all overlapping OR touching closed intervals merged.\nAn empty input returns []. A reversed interval (start > end) anywhere in the input must raise ValueError.\nNumbers are finite. Do not mutate the input or its nested intervals. Preserve the function signature.\nUse only the Python standard library.\n",
        "starter": "def merge_intervals(intervals):\n    intervals.sort()\n    return intervals\n",
        "grader_sha256": "b3036ea85c2e15fc3383e0f96ed78413f85dbaea6e071273ec1e2a16279e7a07",
        "sha256": "199641437cc84e5fa7b68d3d3a83e368a9d4c5ffd061b18ed432a6a8f17a435e"
      },
      {
        "id": "get-path",
        "split": "discovery",
        "instruction": "Repair get_path(data, path, default). Traverse nested dictionaries using a dotted string path.\nA backslash escapes only a dot or another backslash: a\\.b.c addresses key 'a.b' then key 'c'.\nThe empty path, empty segments, trailing backslash, and other escapes are invalid and must raise ValueError.\nValidate the COMPLETE path before traversal, even if an earlier key is missing.\nReturn default for a missing key or a non-dictionary encountered before the end. Return stored None as None.\nDo not mutate inputs. Arguments are ordinary JSON values; path is a string. Preserve the signature.\nUse only the Python standard library.\n",
        "starter": "def get_path(data, path, default):\n    for key in path.split(\".\"):\n        data = data[key]\n    return data\n",
        "grader_sha256": "17ed786f298166de365a54db3086bf7203c6487e394fbb31cada079adf437e69",
        "sha256": "d8ab710e5d8558750d9af0bd862cb5da2626177b89dafc302a1107b840f018cf"
      },
      {
        "id": "toposort",
        "split": "discovery",
        "instruction": "Repair toposort(graph). graph maps each string node to a list of its prerequisite node names.\nInclude nodes mentioned only as prerequisites. Repeated prerequisites count only once.\nReturn a topological ordering, choosing the lexicographically smallest CURRENTLY AVAILABLE node at every step.\nFor example {'a': ['z'], 'b': []} returns ['b', 'z', 'a'].\nRaise ValueError for any cycle including self-loops. Empty input returns []. Do not mutate input dictionaries or lists.\nKeys and prerequisite names are strings, values are lists. Preserve the signature and use only the standard library.\n",
        "starter": "def toposort(graph):\n    return sorted(graph)\n",
        "grader_sha256": "7cdcae527a2540b6fce9eff12c66d24ff8c93df7a90cbd6ec2254bf1dcf5784e",
        "sha256": "53bb2f6dc335ea63c8f4d7c49ecdb63a4860c600c095b6c7f9745e7dd307144e"
      }
    ],
